      "permalink": "the-correct-order-of-the-first-ionization-enthalpies-is--jee-main-chemistry-periodic-table-and-periodicity-5yeqcximf6w841am",
      "content": "The correct order of the first ionization enthalpies is :",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "Ti &lt; Mn &lt; Zn &lt; Ni"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "Zn &lt; Ni &lt; Mn &lt; Ti"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "Mn &lt; Ti &lt; Zn &lt; Ni"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "Ti &lt; Mn &lt; Ni &lt; Zn"
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "D"
      ],
      "explanation": "In a period, from left to right ionization enthalpy increses.\n<br><br>So in period 4, correct order for those 4 elements is\n<br><br>Ti &lt; Mn &lt; Ni &lt; Zn\n<br><br>Exceptions in period 4 are\n<br><br>(1) V(Vanadium) &lt; Ti(Titanium)\n<br><br>(2) Ni(Titanium) &lt; Co(Cobalt)\n<br><br>(3) Ga(Gallium) &lt; Zn(Zinc)\n<br><br>(4) Se(Selenium) &lt; As(Arsenic)"
    }
  ]
